<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odiel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Odiel is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huelva">Huelva</a> province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, rising in the Sierra de Aracena and flowing south to the Atlantic. At Huelva it meets the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-tinto">Río Tinto</a> in a shared estuary, whose marshes, the Marismas del Odiel, are a protected wetland. The island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saltes">Saltés</a> in the estuary was the site of a medieval Islamic town known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-technology">ironworking</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odiel.jpg" alt="Odiel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Lumbanica assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:R%C3%ADo_Odiel.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
